Ms. Gauthier,</div>
<div class="x_x_elementToProof" style="direction:ltr; margin-top:1em; margin-bottom:1em; font-family:Aptos,&quot;Aptos_EmbeddedFont&quot;,&quot;Aptos_MSFontService&quot;,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif; font-size:12pt; color:rgb(0,0,0)">
Both estimates arrived this afternoon, eight minutes apart. My response to both is attached.</div>
<div class="x_x_elementToProof" style="direction:ltr; margin-top:1em; margin-bottom:1em; font-family:Aptos,&quot;Aptos_EmbeddedFont&quot;,&quot;Aptos_MSFontService&quot;,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif; font-size:12pt; color:rgb(0,0,0)">
I dispute both. I am not paying either one, and I am not narrowing either request. I do not pay for records I have a right to see.</div>
<div class="x_x_elementToProof" style="direction:ltr; margin-top:1em; margin-bottom:1em; font-family:Aptos,&quot;Aptos_EmbeddedFont&quot;,&quot;Aptos_MSFontService&quot;,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif; font-size:12pt; color:rgb(0,0,0)">
Neither estimate answers the fee waiver I requested under ORS 192.324(5) on September 5. That request is still pending and it requires a written determination. The authority to make it belongs to the custodian, which is the Director, not to External Relations.</div>
<div class="x_x_elementToProof" style="direction:ltr; margin-top:1em; margin-bottom:1em; font-family:Aptos,&quot;Aptos_EmbeddedFont&quot;,&quot;Aptos_MSFontService&quot;,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif; font-size:12pt; color:rgb(0,0,0)">
Director Sumption is copied here, as she was copied on the request. She is also its subject. Items 1 and 3 seek her own communications. The waiver is hers to grant.</div>
<div class="x_x_elementToProof" style="direction:ltr; margin-top:1em; margin-bottom:1em; font-family:Aptos,&quot;Aptos_EmbeddedFont&quot;,&quot;Aptos_MSFontService&quot;,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif; font-size:12pt; color:rgb(0,0,0)">
One item is not a fee question. On the September 11 request, item 2 is answered &quot;This is not a record we have,&quot; on the same page where item 1 agrees to produce the SharePoint or OneDrive version histories of that document. A version history is a record of saves
 with the date, time, and account for each. If that answer stands, state it as a denial, identify who made it, and state the search performed.</div>
<div class="x_x_elementToProof" style="direction:ltr; margin-top:1em; margin-bottom:1em; font-family:Aptos,&quot;Aptos_EmbeddedFont&quot;,&quot;Aptos_MSFontService&quot;,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif; font-size:12pt; color:rgb(0,0,0)">
There will be no negotiation of scope, no call, and no meeting. Produce the records the public has a right to see. Or don't, and continue to show what kind of institution you are.</div>
<div class="x_x_elementToProof" style="direction:ltr; margin-top:1em; margin-bottom:1em; font-family:Aptos,&quot;Aptos_EmbeddedFont&quot;,&quot;Aptos_MSFontService&quot;,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif; font-size:12pt; color:rgb(0,0,0)">
